course: dictionary
lesson: 5471
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must read the words around them to know which one the writer means. This is called context. Lark is a good example: it can be a bird, a joke, or a silly way to play.
explain: «"Up with the larks" means up very early, a "night owl" stays up late.» Here lark means an early riser, someone who gets up at dawn. The clue is the word early, so the meaning is not about a bird at all.
explain: «Stop larking about!» is what a teacher says to a silly pupil. Larking about is a verb, so it describes an action: playing in a silly, noisy way. When you are not sure, swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A lark is a small brown songbird, such as the skylark, which sings while flying high.
fact: In informal British English, a lark is something done for fun or as a joke: «for a lark» means just for fun.
fact: The verb «lark about» or «lark around» means to play in a silly, noisy way.
fact: «Up with the lark» means getting up very early, like the birds that sing at dawn.
fact: Context means the words around a word, and it is the best clue to which meaning the writer chose.
exercise: «Stop larking about!» What does larking about mean? | Flying high and singing | Reading quietly in the library | Sleeping late in bed | *Playing in a silly, noisy way
exercise: Sam went to the park «for a lark». What does for a lark mean? | To win a prize | To get very tired | To catch a bird | *Just for fun
exercise: What does the phrase «up with the larks» mean? | Up very late at night | Up in a tall tree | *Up very early | Up on a high hill
test: Which bird is known for singing while flying high? | Penguin | Eagle | Owl | *Skylark
test: Which phrase means someone who stays up late? | Lark about | *Night owl | Up with the lark | For a lark
exam: In the sentence «Early risers are larks, and people who stay up late are night owls», what does a night owl do? | Gets up at dawn | *Stays up late | Plays silly games all day | Sings high in the sky
